    "field": "Climate change attribution",
    "problem": "Previous statistical analyses of climate change are difficult to interpret, as they often ignore the dynamic and time-series properties of the variables, making it hard to distinguish a meaningful causal relationship from a coincidental correlation.",
    "method": "The paper uses Granger causality tests on observational and simulated hemispheric temperature records to attribute a detected south-to-north statistical dependence to the climatic effects of anthropogenic greenhouse gases and sulphate aerosols, thus providing evidence for human influence on climate.",
    "task": "The task is to statistically analyze historical temperature records to identify a causal order between the Northern and Southern hemispheres and to attribute this pattern to the climatic effects of anthropogenic greenhouse gases and sulphate aerosols.",
